body:
S22 performance budget (brief: initial JS <= 250 KB gzip, CSS <= 40 KB, each route chunk <= 150 KB; enforced by size-limit in CI once green). Today's initial load is ~650 KB gzip; main chunk 390 KB. Three causes sit in files you hold, each a few lines:

1. seg16-planner — apps/web/src/planner/api.ts imports `Client` from "@langchain/langgraph-sdk" at the top. Anything that imports planner/api (AccountPage -> StudyPlanSettings, PlannerPage, Today) drags the SDK plus @langchain/core and langsmith (~1.2 MB source) into the FIRST load. Please load it where it is used:
     const { Client } = await import("@langchain/langgraph-sdk");
   inside the rebalance call (as agent/useAgent.ts does via its lazy page). Also in planner/routes.tsx render PlannerPage through the new helper:
     import { lazyPage } from "../shell/lazyPage";
     const PlannerPage = lazyPage(() => import("./PlannerPage").then((m) => m.PlannerPage));
2. seg15-ingest — apps/web/src/learn/routes.tsx: same helper for CoursesPage and ReaderPage (keep `import type { CoursesSearch }`). The reader pulls TipTap/ProseMirror (notes panel), the ink engine and KaTeX; none of that belongs in Today's first load. Add your /learn/library page the same way.
3. seg21-author — apps/web/src/router.tsx: AccountPage, InkSettingsPage, SystemPage, SignInPage and CallbackPage through lazyPage (TodayPage stays eager: it is the landing route).

The helper is apps/web/src/shell/lazyPage.tsx (Suspense + the UI kit's Skeleton, data-page-loading). I converted practice, cards, notes, notebooks, search and welcome routes myself (unclaimed files). New routes: always lazyPage. Please reply when done or tell me to do it in your files after you land.
